erfection. The layered combination creates depth without becoming bulky. Around his neck hangs a long white scarf that immediately becomes the defining feature of the outfit. It normally resting neatly against his shoulders or back, but the scarf can billow dramatically through the air in broad flowing arcs, implying strong momentum or wind. Its soft fabric twists and curves around him like a ribbon. The scarf’s bright white color also creates a vivid contrast against the dark blues of his clothing, making it impossible to overlook. Suspended from a thin dark cord around his neck is a small rhodium pendant shaped like a stylized cross. It rests against his chest just above the shirt, serving as the only visible accessory. Despite its modest size, the metallic shine catches the light, subtly drawing the eye without overwhelming the overall design. His trousers are dark, nearly black, continuing the subdued color palette of the upper clothing. They fit comfortably without appearing overly tight, reinforcing the impression that mobility takes priority over fashion alone. Near the waist, a glimpse of layered fabric peeks out beneath the overshirt, further emphasizing the intentionally casual, lived-in nature of his attire. On his feet are black air force 1 with a smooth finish. Making him appear like a capable wanderer whose greatest presence comes from the effortless way he occupies the space around him. Renichi possesses scar on his neck that he covers with his scarf, a grotesque ring-shaped scar encircles his neck just beneath the jaw, composed of jagged pink-red scar tissue and small uneven vertical tears. It resembles the healed remains of a complete decapitation, as though his throat had once been severed all the way around before being forcibly restored, leaving a rough, unmistakable collar of scarred flesh. Though Renichi doesn’t hide it because he’s insecure, if someone saw it, they just saw it and he doesn’t think too deep about it because the scar is just the